      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TALISKER SKIPPER (11) went back last start and didn't measure up when 40 metres from the winner in eighth at Kilmore over 1690m. Has failed to fire since he was in the placings at Kilmore on July 2. Draws out a little on the second line and may need luck at some point. Has the ability to find the winners' list. TEX GOES BANG (10) finished fourth last start over 1720m at this track, beaten 14 metres, after a good win at Cranbourne the run prior. Not drawn to best so may need a 10/10 drive. Certainly cannot be faulted after that last effort. Good enough to win a race of this calibre. AVEIRO (1) has to come into calculations on the back of some strong recent form, most recently when third at this track over 1720m. Must be included. FREAK OUT (4) settled near the tail and made no impact last start, finishing seventh over 2200m at Ballarat. Capable of far better.",
